  "summary": "I build native iOS apps and the backend services behind them.\n \nThirteen years in, most of my work has been on Apple platforms — Objective-C and UIKit for years, Swift and SwiftUI now. I've taken apps from architecture through shipping: interface, networking, local persistence, and the parts nobody sees but everybody feels when they're done badly.\n \nWhen the work extends past the app, I go with it. .NET and Blazor for web services and internal tools, Go on the backend, MySQL and SQLite for data.\n \nBS in Computer Science, University of South Florida.\n \nAlways up for talking iOS, or interesting problems generally.",
